+ * Review's finding, and it is the sharpest one in phase 4: nothing asserted that
+ * the read model applies either gate event. Every decider test hand-builds its
+ * read model, so a projector that dropped `gateRevision` would pass all eleven of
+ * them while every write after the first re-allocated revision 1 — which is
+ * precisely the failure the revision mechanism exists to prevent, invisible to
+ * the suite that was meant to protect it.
+ *
+ * These read the mark back out of a projected model, so a projector that forgets
+ * it fails here.
+ */
